<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3 </span>Addition Results</h3>

<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A4.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ D.2 Implementation Details ‣ Appendix D Detailed Results ‣ RESTRAIN: From Spurious Votes to Signals — Self-Driven RL with Self-Penalization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> and <a href="#A4.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ D.3 Addition Results ‣ Appendix D Detailed Results ‣ RESTRAIN: From Spurious Votes to Signals — Self-Driven RL with Self-Penalization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> show full results of our RESTRAIN on nine benchmarks. Results show that our method can outperform all unsupervised methods on both Qwen3-4B-Base and Octothinker Hybrid 8B base models with two different training datasets.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T6" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A4.T6.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 6</span>: </span><span id="A4.T6.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">The table shows the evaluation results of training Qwen3-4B-Base on <span id="A4.T6.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">5k Synthetic S1k dataset</span>, all results(%) are averaged over 16 seeds. The best results are highlighted in <span id="A4.T6.6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E8F1FF;">bold<span id="A4.T6.6.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">.</span></span></span></figcaption>
<table id="A4.T6.7" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A4.T6.7.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T6.7.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.75pt 4.0pt;">Model</td>
<td id="A4.T6.7.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.75pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="A4.T6.7.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
