</section>
<section id="A7" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix G </span>Study of Hyperparameter Negative Advantage Offset <math id="A7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> and Majority Count Threshold <math id="A7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math></h2>

<div id="A7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we examine how the negative-advantage offset <math id="A7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> and the majority-count threshold <math id="A7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> influence performance. The offset <math id="A7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> scales the penalty applied to low-consensus rollouts; if set too high, it over-penalizes the policy and induces a sharp accuracy decline. The threshold <math id="A7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> decides which prompts are treated as low-consensus: a strict threshold discards many informative examples and hurts accuracy, while an overly loose threshold admits noisy cases and weakens the intended penalization. Appropriate, balanced choices of <math id="A7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> suppress noise without sacrificing useful signal.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A7.T8" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A7.T8.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 8</span>: </span><span id="A7.T8.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Results on Different Negative rollout Penalty.<span id="A7.T8.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> The table shows the evaluation results of training Qwen3-4B-Base on </span>14k DAPO-Math dataset<span id="A7.T8.7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> by varying the negative advantage offset, all results(%) are averaged over 16 seeds. The best results are highlighted in </span><span id="A7.T8.7.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E8F1FF;">bold<span id="A7.T8.7.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">.</span></span></span></figcaption>
